 "title": "SYSOUT forms (class, (class,,form), DEST), DD DUMMY and COND=EVEN / COND=ONLY on a step",
 "category": "jcl",
 "issue": 4891,
 "shapes": [
  "BDLD jcl/BDLDSYS.jcl SYS010: DD SYSOUT=(A,,STD1), SYSOUT=Z,DEST=NYC01, SYSOUT=*, and a DD DUMMY",
  "BDLD jcl/BDLDSYS.jcl SYS020: EXEC COND=EVEN; SYS030: COND=((4,LT,SYS010),ONLY)"
 ],
 "asserts": "Each DD with a SYSOUT parameter is a jcl_dds fact whose sysout is the operand as coded, parentheses and omitted subparameters kept ((A,,STD1), Z, *); DEST and other keywords are not part of it. A DD DUMMY is dummy true with no dsn. The cond of a step is the COND operand as coded: EVEN, or ((4,LT,SYS010),ONLY); EVEN / ONLY are interpreted before the return-code tests and decide whether the step runs after an earlier abend.",
 "citations": [
  {
   "doc": "z/OS MVS JCL Reference (z/OS 2.1.0)",
   "section": "DD statement > SYSOUT parameter",
